WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.826
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:09.501
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:16.180
Unit four: Technology News. Today you will talk about plans and launches with 'is set to' and 'is due to'.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.249
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.944
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:25.808
Innovation.

7
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:30.372
Innovation means a new idea, method or invention.

8
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:33.656
Innovation drives the technology industry.

9
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.937
Your turn. Say: Innovation.

10
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.778
Innovation.

11
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:42.239
Launch.

12
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.445
Launch means the first time a product is shown or sold.

13
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.479
The launch attracted thousands of customers.

14
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.480
Your turn. Say: Launch.

15
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:56.300
Launch.

16
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:57.889
Startup.

17
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:02.253
Startup means a new company, often based on a new idea.

18
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.000
A Phnom Penh startup created the app.

19
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:08.281
Your turn. Say: Startup.

20
00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.111
Startup.

21
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:13.723
Device.

22
00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:18.237
Device means a small machine made for a particular purpose.

23
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.117
This device charges in ten minutes.

24
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.473
Your turn. Say: Device.

25
00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:28.300
Device.

26
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:30.353
Software update.

27
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.987
Software update means a new version of a program that improves it.

28
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:38.140
The software update fixed the security problem.

29
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.878
Your turn. Say: Software update.

30
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:46.141
Software update.

31
00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:47.803
Breakthrough.

32
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:52.163
Breakthrough means an important discovery that solves a problem.

33
00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.993
Scientists announced a battery breakthrough.

34
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:58.027
Your turn. Say: Breakthrough.

35
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:01.856
Breakthrough.

36
00:02:02.617 --> 00:02:03.629
Industry.

37
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:08.149
Industry means all the companies that make one kind of product.

38
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.435
The technology industry employs millions.

39
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:14.702
Your turn. Say: Industry.

40
00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.556
Industry.

41
00:02:19.317 --> 00:02:20.283
Consumer.

42
00:02:21.283 --> 00:02:24.479
Consumer means a person who buys goods or services.

43
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:27.652
Consumers want cheaper, faster devices.

44
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.624
Your turn. Say: Consumer.

45
00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.503
Consumer.

46
00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.881
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:44.923
Visal, this article says a new phone 'is set to launch next month'. What does 'set to' mean?

48
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:54.358
It means the event is planned and expected. 'Is due to' is similar: the company is due to announce the device on Monday.

49
00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.590
Is it certain?

50
00:02:57.683 --> 00:03:05.000
It is a strong plan, but technology news also uses 'is likely to' and 'could' when a launch is not confirmed.

51
00:03:06.117 --> 00:03:08.290
Why do headlines love these phrases?

52
00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:17.005
They are short and neutral. They tell consumers what is coming without promising it, which is important in a fast-moving industry.

53
00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.853
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.717 --> 00:03:24.551
Grammar focus: Future news with is set to and is due to.

55
00:03:24.851 --> 00:03:26.037
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.493
The startup is set to launch its app next month.

57
00:03:30.383 --> 00:03:32.882
The new device is due to go on sale on Monday.

58
00:03:33.783 --> 00:03:35.853
The update is likely to fix the problem.

59
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:43.957
Use is set to / is due to + base verb for planned events, and is likely to for probable ones. Do not add 'will' after them.

60
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:48.158
Be careful! Don't say: The app is set to will launch.

61
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.518
Say: The app is set to launch.

62
00:03:52.818 --> 00:03:54.724
Do not add will after is set to.

63
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:58.534
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:00.892
A Busy Week in Tech.

65
00:04:01.192 --> 00:04:05.014
This week the technology industry is full of news about innovation.

66
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:11.494
A local startup is set to launch a learning app, and a new device is due to reach shops on Monday.

67
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:17.576
Meanwhile, a software update is likely to improve security on millions of phones.

68
00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:22.853
Researchers also announced a battery breakthrough that could last twice as long.

69
00:04:23.867 --> 00:04:28.513
For consumers, each launch brings new choices and new questions about cost.

70
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.323
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:34.183 --> 00:04:36.763
The startup blank to launch its app next month.

72
00:04:37.063 --> 00:04:40.833
A, is set. B, set. C, will set.

73
00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.239
The answer is A: is set.

74
00:04:47.383 --> 00:04:50.323
A new version of a program is a software blank.

75
00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:54.033
A, update. B, device. C, industry.

76
00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.938
The answer is A: update.

77
00:05:01.083 --> 00:05:04.302
An important discovery that solves a problem is a blank.

78
00:05:04.602 --> 00:05:08.279
A, launch. B, breakthrough. C, consumer.

79
00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:13.868
The answer is B: breakthrough.

80
00:05:15.017 --> 00:05:16.784
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:17.084 --> 00:05:24.998
A, The device is due to goes on sale.. B, The device is due to go on sale.. C, The device due to go on sale..

82
00:05:28.533 --> 00:05:32.042
The answer is B: The device is due to go on sale..

83
00:05:33.183 --> 00:05:36.147
According to the reading, the update is likely to improve…

84
00:05:36.447 --> 00:05:40.390
A, price. B, security. C, battery colour.

85
00:05:43.933 --> 00:05:46.200
The answer is B: security.

86
00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.644
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:55.073
What recent piece of technology news have you heard about?

88
00:06:03.883 --> 00:06:05.662
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:05.962 --> 00:06:26.255
I recently read that a local startup is set to launch a mobile app for farmers. The app is expected to show market prices and weather forecasts in Khmer. I think it is an exciting innovation because many farmers do not have reliable information. If it works well, it could help them earn more.

90
00:06:26.555 --> 00:06:28.265
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:34.566
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future news with is set to and is due to.

92
00:06:34.866 --> 00:06:38.725
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

93
00:06:39.025 --> 00:06:41.620
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.514
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

